[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67617,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary cardiac (extranodal) diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) arises in the heart, although it may extend to adjacent tissues.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67618,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9680/3 Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67619,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A81.Z Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67620,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67621,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67622,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The right atrium is the most common site. Roughly one&nbsp;third of all cases involve the pericardium {20922788}. Valvular involvement is rare {23849494}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67623,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms vary with the size and location of involvement. Dyspnoea, chest pain, and heart failure are frequent {20922788}. Pulmonary embolism has also been reported {6305485; 10559123}. Arrhythmias and sudden cardiac death may also occur {17410366; 15782345}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>On echocardiography, cardiac lymphoma usually manifests as hypoechogenic infiltration of the myocardium, often with pericardial effusion {27265603}. CT and MRI can provide additional detail. Endomyocardial biopsy may lead to histological diagnosis (and treatment) without thoracotomy {23248217}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67624,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary cardiac lymphomas (the majority of which are DLBCL) account for &lt;&nbsp;2% of primary cardiac neoplasms in surgical series {22977025; 20922788}, with an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 2:1 {20922788}. The median age is 63&nbsp;years, but occurrence in a 9-year-old has been reported {12447675}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67625,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67626,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Perhaps the most notable feature of cardiac DLBCL is the high frequency of lymphoma types associated with impaired immunity. These types include EBV-associated DLBCL, DLBCL associated with chronic inflammation {19351686; 20139760; 24060945}, and fibrin-associated large B-cell lymphoma {22982895; 20139760}. Primary cardiac low-grade B-cell lymphomas also occur {3543244; 19279985; 18297519}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67627,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, primary cardiac lymphomas are multinodular grey-white coalescing masses that can involve any or all tissue layer(s). They may also extend to the great arteries.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67628,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular monotony, dyscohesion, and large cell size are hallmarks of DLBCL. Immunophenotyping is critical, especially to characterize the cell of origin (germinal-centre B&nbsp;cell vs activated B&nbsp;cell), MYC/BCL2 coexpression, and EBV status.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67629,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytological evaluation, particularly in cases with pericardial effusion, can be diagnostic {2011932}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67630,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>MYC</em> and <em>BCL2</em> FISH and EBV in&nbsp;situ studies assist in classification. A molecular classification for DLBCL, based on whole-exome sequencing, has been proposed {29713087; 29641966}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67631,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Large B-cell lymphoma involving the heart/pericardium with no or minor extracardiac component</li>\r\n<li>Mature B-cell immunophenotype (as described above)</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T17:52:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67632,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is according to the Lugano classification, a modification of the Ann Arbor staging system {25113753}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-30T18:21:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67633,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "<p>The prognosis is typically poor, especially if myocardial rupture occurs {3609049}. Response to chemotherapy is generally on par with that of DLBCL at extracardiac sites {20922788}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T17:52:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]